foundation.question_text:
$8$ points are marked on the circumference of a circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2.2);
\fill (90:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (45:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (0:2.2) circle (2pt) node[right] {$C$};
\fill (-45:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$D$};
\fill (-90:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (-135:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$F$};
\fill (180:2.2) circle (2pt) node[left] {$G$};
\fill (135:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many straight lines can be drawn by joining pairs of these points?

development.question_text:
$9$ points lie in a plane such that no three points are collinear.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill (-2,1.6) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (-0.5,2.1) circle (2pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (1.8,1.7) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$C$};
\fill (2.2,0.2) circle (2pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (1.4,-1.5) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$E$};
\fill (-0.2,-2.1) circle (2pt) node[below] {$F$};
\fill (-1.9,-1.6) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$G$};
\fill (-2.2,0) circle (2pt) node[left] {$H$};
\fill (0.2,0.4) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$I$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many distinct triangles can be formed with vertices at these points?

mastery.question_text:
$12$ points are marked on the circumference of a circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2.2);
\fill (90:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (60:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (30:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$C$};
\fill (0:2.2) circle (2pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (-30:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$E$};
\fill (-60:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$F$};
\fill (-90:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below] {$G$};
\fill (-120:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$H$};
\fill (-150:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$I$};
\fill (180:2.2) circle (2pt) node[left] {$J$};
\fill (150:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$K$};
\fill (120:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$L$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many sets of $4$ points can be chosen to form a convex quadrilateral?
